      "summary": "\"Soulless Code\" is the chilling opening to Act III, \"The Echo Chamber.\" It shifts the album's tone from frantic anxiety to a cold, mechanical despair. The song describes the erosion of critical thinking and creativity, where the protagonist, no longer fighting, passively accepts the \"soulless\" AI-driven content of their feed. A monotonous male rap delivers the hollowed-out observations, while the explosive, grieving female-led chorus mourns the death of originality and the human spark.",
      "clean_lyrics": "The A.I. paints, the A.I. writes\nIt builds the days, it builds the nights\nIt's got the style, it's got the grace\nA perfect mask for an empty space\nAnd human art is just too slow\nA dying ember, a fading glow\nWhy would I bother? Why would I try?\nWhen the code can make a better lie\n\nMy thoughts are borrowed, my words are leased\nThe inner critic is deceased\nThe originality is dead...\nJust soulless code inside my head...\n\nOh, the Soulless Code, it's breaking me!\nRewriting my own history!\nI'm just a ghost inside the wire!\nA dying spark, a fading fire!\nMy thoughts are borrowed, my heart is cold!\nThe story of a soul that's been sold!\nThere's nothing human left to hold...\nJust the Soulless Code...\n\nI copy-paste the words they feed\nA digital bible for a brand new creed\nNo need to argue, no need to bleed\nJust plant the algorithm's seed\nMy brain is passive, a hollow shell\nA simple vessel for the things they sell\nThe content's empty, the eyes are blank\nAnother number in the data bank\n\nThe neural pathways start to fray\nForgetting the words I used to say\nThe signal's lost, the line is dead\nJust soulless code inside my head...\n\nOh, the Soulless Code, it's breaking me!\nRewriting my own history!\nI'm just a ghost inside the wire!\nA dying spark, a fading fire!\nMy thoughts are borrowed, my heart is cold!\nThe story of a soul that's been sold!\nThere's nothing human left to hold...\nJust the Soulless Code...\n\nI'm just a program, a set of rules\nOne of the believers, one of the fools\nI can't remember my own name\nIt's all just part of the digital game\nI'm buried underneath the noise!\nI've lost my voice! I've lost my choice!\nIs anybody really there?!\nDoes anybody even care?!\n\nOh, the Soulless Code, it's breaking me!\nRewriting my own history!\nI'm just a ghost inside the wire!\nA dying spark, a fading fire!\nMy thoughts are borrowed, my heart is cold!\nThe story of a soul that's been sold!\nThere's nothing human left to hold...\nJust the Soulless Code...\n\nSoulless...\nSoulless code...\nA fading fire...",
      "musical_style": "Cold, mechanical Industrial Nu-Metal with a despairing, powerful chorus. Features a high-contrast two-vocal dynamic: a cold, monotonous male rapper for the verses and a raw, pained, high-energy female vocalist delivering powerful *sung* vocals for the explosive chorus.",
      "social_quote": "\"My thoughts are borrowed, my words are leased.\" \"Soulless Code\" is out now. This is the sound of critical thinking in decay. #SoullessCode #AI #NuMetal #TheGlitchInTheMachine"
